# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on at least one development machine, which rewrites LF
# to CRLF on checkout. For most sources that is harmless, but two trees are
# content under test rather than code you edit, and a silent conversion there
# changes what a test observes:
#
#   examples/          demo fixtures. tests/test_codeagent_newlines.py asserts a
#                      fixture is LF before replaying an edit against it, because
#                      the bug it guards against was an edit rewriting every line
#                      ending in a file. A CRLF checkout makes that precondition
#                      false and the guard unrunnable.
#   skill_library/     authored instruction text whose bytes are digested at
#                      snapshot. Stable endings keep a digest comparable across
#                      machines.
#
# Pinned to LF so a checkout produces the bytes the repository actually holds.
examples/** text eol=lf
src/engine/skill_library/** text eol=lf
